  "title": "Wild Karoo",
  "notes": "**THE VALLEY v4.15.0 \"WILD KAROO\"** \u2014 Ionity (Pty) Ltd\n\nInstall or update with one small file: **TheValley_Setup.exe** (below). It downloads the game itself and never re-downloads what you already have. Every piece is verified when it arrives and every installed file is verified as it is unpacked (\"Verifying items ...\"), so a damaged file stops the setup instead of breaking the game.\n\n**Play together**\n- PvP between players: Kernel against Ashclaw, every blow checked by the World Server.\n- Duels: `/duel <name>` \u2014 a banner drops, a 20 m ring, 3-2-1, fight to 1 HP. No death, no level lost; the Valley hears who won. Leave the ring for 5 s and you forfeit.\n- Line of sight: ranged spells and shots need a clear line \u2014 hills, cliffs, walls and buildings block them.\n- Rejoins the World Server by itself once you are signed in. Ping shown bottom-right.\n\n**The Wild Karoo**\n- Vegetation packs across the whole valley; real zebra, cow, fox and more; photoscanned pebble fields.\n- Ore veins with real copper, iron, gold and mana-crystal ore.\n- Draw distance by object size (DRAW DISTANCE slider) \u2014 big help on weaker PCs.\n\n**Classes**\n- Rogues use Energy (starts at 30 of 150, refills 10 a second); Rage builds 1:1 from damage taken and 1:2 from damage dealt.\n- New spell effects, casting animations and hit effects; champions talk (\"I need more mana!\", \"Ouch!\").\n- Towers have less HP and grow stronger for every town your side holds.\n\n**Feel**\n- Controls no longer stick: mouse smoothing off, no more micro-freezes on heavy hits, full speed straight after a cast.\n- Resolution is a dropdown in settings.\n",
